  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal obligations to Women-Owned Small Business set-asides total $581M. Award activity so far includes 1,978 awards and an average award size of $294K. Obligations fell 54.1% year over year, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The program reached $1.3B in both FY24 and FY25, after a rise from $856M in FY21, $934M in FY22, and $1.2B in FY23. The drop to $581M in FY26 to date shows a sharp pullback in obligations compared with the two most recent full fiscal years. Buyers, vendors, and industry concentrations below reflect only the FY2026 to date obligations and the partial-year nature of the totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are WOSB set-aside obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for the largest share at $292M. The next largest buyers are the Department of Homeland Security at $71.6M and the Department of Commerce at $50.1M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $36M and the Department of Justice at $23.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors capture the most WOSB set-aside dollars?",
        "body": "Engineering Services and Other Computer Related Services each received $103M. Top vendors in FY2026 to date include INTELLECT SOLUTIONS, LLC at $18.5M and DTECHLOGIC LLC at $17.4M, followed by FCN, INC. at $16.4M. Several other vendors range from $12.8M down to $10.5M, and other industry categories with meaningful totals include Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $39.5M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $29.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
